    </Option>
  </Option>
  <Option name="help" type="Map">
    <Option value="Lorenzo Moretti" name="ALG_CREATOR" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;>&#xa;&lt;html>&lt;head>&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; />&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;>&#xa;p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }&#xa;&lt;/style>&lt;/head>&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'.AppleSystemUIFont'; font-size:13pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-size:18pt; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;>ShaLIA - Shallow Landslides Initiation Assessment&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14pt; font-weight:600;&quot;>WARNING! All vector and raster layers in INPUT must have the SAME PROJECTION. The raster files must have the SAME RESOLUTION and the SAME EXTENSION too!!!!&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-size:14pt; font-weight:600;&quot;>WARNING! IF EACH OF YOUR RASTER FILES HAS A BIG SIZE (E.G., MORE THAN 5 GB), THIS MODEL GENERATES A LOT OF HUGE TEMPORARY FILES: YOU MUST HAVE A LOT OF SPACE ON YOUR HARD DISK (e.g.: eight 5 GB raster files generate about 150 GB of temporary files).&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>This model works in QGIS 3.42 and later and QGIS 4.2 and later.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>The model consists of 194 algorithms, including 169 native to QGIS, 22 GDAL, and 3 SAGA.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>The only plugin required is “&lt;/span>&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/baswein/qgis-processing-saga-nextgenhttps://github.com/baswein/qgis-processing-saga-nextgen&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline; color:#0068da;&quot;>Processing Saga NextGen Provider&lt;/span>&lt;/a>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>” vers. 1.3&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:'Mona Sans VF','-apple-system','BlinkMacSystemFont','Segoe UI','Noto Sans Backtick Fix','Noto Sans','Helvetica','Arial','sans-serif','Apple Color Emoji','Segoe UI Emoji'; font-size:14px; font-weight:600; color:#1f2328;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>The susceptibility map is created from some initial data that are processed to produce 7 raster layers of the area, each with its own weight, which will determine the final map.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;>INPUT&lt;/span> &lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>a) &lt;/span>a raster file of&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>ORIGINAL DTM&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>, the Digital Terrain Model with the best resolution with elevations in meters with decimal values;&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>b)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> a vector file for the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>LANDSLIDE AREA, &lt;/span>a calibration subset of all landslide areas;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>c)&lt;/span> a raster file of the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>SLOPE&lt;/span> of the area (it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>d)&lt;/span> a raster file of the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>ASPECT&lt;/span> of the area (it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>e)&lt;/span> a raster file of the &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>LAND COVER&lt;/span> of the area (it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>) -&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> &lt;/span>&lt;a href=&quot;https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/corine-land-cover&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline; color:#0068da;&quot;>Corine Land Cover&lt;/span>&lt;/a>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> is good source but &lt;/span>&lt;a href=&quot;https://land.copernicus.eu/en/products/coastal-zones&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline; color:#0068da;&quot;>Coastal Zones of Corine Land Cover&lt;/span>&lt;/a>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;> &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>is much better if your area is near the sea. You have to choose which field of the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>level code&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> of the land cover. From Level 1 with an indication of the main soil categories up to Level 5 where the detail of land use is very high. In our case Level 3 is a very good level of detail&lt;/span>;&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>f)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> a raster file of the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>SOIL THICKNESS MAP&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>STM&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - with &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-style:italic; text-decoration: underline;&quot;>values in meters&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> &lt;/span>(a Raster file you already have, or it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>g)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> a raster layer of the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>GEO&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>LOGICAL MAP &lt;/span>of the area (it's  created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>h)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> a raster file of the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>TERRAIN RUGGEDNESS INDEX&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>TRI&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - of the area &lt;/span>(it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>i)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> a raster file of the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>TOPOGRAPHIC WETNESS INDEX&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>TWI&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> - of the area &lt;/span>(it's created from the previous model &lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>ShaLIA_pre&lt;/span>);&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>j)&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> If the DTM grid is much larger than the landslide areas within the grid, it must be selected, &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>VERY LARGE RASTER GRID&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; selected. For example, if the DTM has a resolution of 100x100 meters (area of 10,000 m²) and the landslide areas are much smaller, e.g., 100 or 200 m², the flag can be selected for a more accurate result. If, on the other hand, the DTM has a much lower resolution, e.g., 10x10 meters (area of 100 m²), the flag should not be selected: &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>VERY LARGE RASTER GRID&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; not selected. Choose based on the area data: it's a your choice.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600;&quot;>k)&lt;/span> Usually all 7 models &lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>(Geological, Land Cover, Slope, Aspect, Soil Thickness, Terrain Ruggedness Index and Topographic Wetness Index) &lt;/span>are used to &lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>produce the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;>Susceptibility Map&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> (&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>SELECT RASTER FOR CALCULATION&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; ALL) but it's possible to exclude one raster model from the calculation: in this way the program use only 6 models. A more precise validation of the final map with 6 models and not 7 is useful using the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>ROC Analysis&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> programme afterwards. You can choose the model to be excluded for final processing by selecting it in &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>SELECT RASTER FOR CALCULATION&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; EXCLUDE ONLY ONE and select in &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>WHICH RASTER&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; the raster model to be excluded. Otherwise you can select only ONE model raster for the calculation selecting it in &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>SELECT RASTER FOR CALCULATION&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; ONLY ONE and select in &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>WHICH RASTER&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> --&amp;gt; the raster model to be calculated: in this case the final map is derived only from ONE raster model. This part is only for statistical data.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:600; text-decoration: underline;&quot;>OUTPUT&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;>In the output there are many Excel files and two raster: the Excel file for any raster model with all data inside. The most important is &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>FULL_DATA,&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> and the &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600;&quot;>SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> in two versions, &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>original&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> and &lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial'; font-weight:600; font-style:italic;&quot;>reclassified&lt;/span>&lt;span style=&quot; font-family:'Arial';&quot;> from 1, very low susceptibility, to 5, very high susceptibility.&lt;/span>&lt;/p>&lt;/body>&lt;/html>" name="ALG_DESC" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="lorenzo.moretti@enea.it" name="ALG_HELP_CREATOR" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="4.0" name="ALG_VERSION" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;>&#xa;&lt;html>&lt;head>&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; />&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;>&#xa;p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }&#xa;&lt;/style>&lt;/head>&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'.AppleSystemUIFont'; font-size:13pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;>&#xa;&lt;p style=&quot;-qt-paragraph-type:empty; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;>&lt;br />&lt;/p>&lt;/body>&lt;/html>" name="EXAMPLES" type="QString"/>
    <Option name="HELP_URL" type="invalid"/>
    <Option value="The susceptibility map is created from some initial data that are processed to produce 7 raster layers of the area, each with its own weight, which will determine the final map: a complex calculation whose timing is depending on the processor used&#xa;&#xa;&#xa;" name="SHORT_DESCRIPTION" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector layer of the AREAS in which the highest elevation is to be found.&#xa;ATTENTION ---> &quot;ID_LIP&quot; is the mandatory name of the field for the identification of any area" name="areas_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the ASPECT of the area (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre)" name="aspect_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The field with the numerical code of the GEOLOGICAL area" name="category__geological_code" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The field of the Level of the type of soil. In Level 1 there are the main soil categories while in Level 5 the soil categories are very detailed. Level 3 is a good choice. Must be an integer number" name="category__level_code" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The Lithological code field. Must be an integer number" name="category__lithological_code" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Lithological code" name="category__lithology_code" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="E' il DEM ORIGINALE quello su cui si basa l'intero studio. Deve avere una risoluzione molto bassa, ad esempio 1 m/pixel, ed è preferibile che abbia i valori con decimali per una migliore precisione." name="deminiziodecimale" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Inserire la risoluzione del DEM ORIGINALE in metri per pixel" name="demrisoluzione" type="QString"/>
    <Option name="descrizione" type="invalid"/>
    <Option value="Choose which parameter to exclude from the final calculation or use all parameters, none excluded. Useful for validating the model with the ROC Analysis programme.&#xa;A more precise validation of the final map with 6 models and not 7 is useful using the ROC Analysis programme afterwards" name="exclude_one_parameter_from_the_calculation" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The original SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP without reclassification but with logarithm value. You can see the value under zero (no susceptibility) and above zero (susceptibility)" name="gdal:rastercalculator_13:SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP logn original" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The original SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP with a different value in any pixel" name="gdal:rastercalculator_2:SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP original" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of SLOPE" name="gdal:rastercalculator_4:SLOPE" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of ASPECT" name="gdal:rastercalculator_5:ASPECT" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The original version of the SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP" name="gdal:rastercalculator_5:SUSCEPTIBILITY_MAP_original" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of LITHYOLOGY at the start" name="gdal:rasterize_2:LIT_class_start" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of LAND COVER at the start" name="gdal:rasterize_3:CZLC_class_start" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of LAND COVER at the start" name="gdal:rasterize_3:LC_class_start" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of ROUGHNESS" name="gdal:triterrainruggednessindex_1:TRI" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The original SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP without reclassification" name="gdal:warpreproject_11:SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP original" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The final SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP - Level 1 to 5 (from 'no susceptibility' to 'high susceptibility')" name="gdal:warpreproject_12:SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP reclassified from 1 (low) to 5 (high susceptibility)" name="gdal:warpreproject_13:SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster of WETNESS" name="gdal:warpreproject_1:TWI" type="QString"/>
    <Option name="gdal:warpreproject_1:warpthick" type="invalid"/>
    <Option value="The vector polygons of GEOLOGICAL MAP of the area" name="geological_map_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster layer of the GEOLOGICAL MAP of the area (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre);" name="geology_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster layer of GROUND THICKNESS MAP with the best risolution in meters" name="ground_thickness_map_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The INVENTORY point of the landslide of the area" name="inventory_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the LAND COVER of the area - Corine Land Cover is good source but Coastal Zones of Corine Land Cover is much better if your area in near the sea, at a maximum distance of 10 km. You have to choose which field of the level code of the land cover. From Level 1 with an indication of the main soil categories up to Level 5 where the detail of land use is very high. In our case Level 3 is a very good level of detail (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre) &#xa;" name="land_cover_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector layer of LAND COVER with the categories of land use (Corine Land Cover is a good source): levels of categories go from code 1 (greatest area) to 5 (more detailed ares)" name="land_cover_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector polygons of LANDSLIDE AREA for calibration - a subset of all Landslide Areas" name="landslide_area_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="CALIBRATION and VALIDATION points were randomly selected from a previous model" name="lip__calibration_subset" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="CALIBRATION and VALIDATION points were randomly selected from a previous model" name="lip__validation_subset" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector layer of LITHOLOGICAL MAP with the data. The Lithology Code field must also be chosen: must be an integer number" name="lithological_map_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector points with the highest quote in the area.  Only 1 point for each area. Any point has many features of the area in different fields. The SOIL THICKNESS MAP permits to calculate the Volume of any area in m3 in two ways:&#xa;&#xa;- the sum of the volumes of each pixel in the grid (&quot;VolumeSTsum&quot;);&#xa;- the area of the polygon multiplied by the average thickness of the area (&quot;VolumeSTmean&quot;).&#xa;&#xa;The LITHOLOGICAL MAP permits to extract the value of the Unit Weigth of the each area.&#xa;&#xa;This file is ready for the script 2, the next one." name="native:assignprojection_1:1-Max Value Points" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector points with the highest quote in the area. Only 1 point for any area. The SOIL THICKNESS MAP permits to calculate the Volume of any area in m3, in two ways: one is the sum of any volume of the cell (&quot;VolumeTsum&quot;) and one is the product of area of vector polygon X mean of thickness of the area (&quot;VolumeTmean&quot;)" name="native:assignprojection_1:1-Source Area Features" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The Statistic data of the area" name="native:assignprojection_1:DATA_STAT" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector points with the highest quote in the area.  Only 1 point for each area. Any point has many features of the area in different fields. &#xa;The SOIL THICKNESS MAP permits to calculate the Volume (for script 3 and 4) of any area in m3 in two ways:&#xa;- the sum of the volumes of each pixel in the grid (&quot;VolumeSTsum&quot;);&#xa;- the area of the polygon multiplied by the average thickness of the area (&quot;VolumeSTmean&quot;).&#xa;&#xa;The LITHOLOGICAL MAP permits to extract the value of the Unit Weigth of the each area (for script 4)&#xa;&#xa;This file is ready for the script 2, the next one." name="native:assignprojection_1:ShaLPA1 - Landslide Identification Points" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector points with the highest quote in the area.  Only 1 point for each area. Any point has many features of the area in different fields. &#xa;The SOIL THICKNESS MAP permits to calculate the Volume (for script 3 and 4) of any area in m3 in two ways:&#xa;- the sum of the volumes of each pixel in the grid (&quot;VolumeSTsum&quot;);&#xa;- the area of the polygon multiplied by the average thickness of the area (&quot;VolumeSTmean&quot;).&#xa;&#xa;The LITHOLOGICAL MAP permits to extract the value of the Unit Weigth of the each area (for script 4)&#xa;&#xa;This file is ready for the script 2, the next one." name="native:assignprojection_1:ShaLPA1- Landslide Identification Points" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The vector layer with the points with the highest elevation within each area: one point per area.&#xa;&#xa;IMPORTANT: One of the fields present will be &quot;ID_PIFF,&quot; the identifier taken from the area.  Each point carries with it the identifier of its own area." name="native:assignprojection_1:finalpoints" type="QString"/>
    <Option name="native:assignprojection_2:1-Max Value Points" type="invalid"/>
