    <Option value="The ORIGINAL DEM, the starting DEM with the best resolution and, if possible, with elevations in meters with decimal values" name="original_dem_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster layer of ORIGINAL DTM with the best risolution in meters" name="original_dtm_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Le aree delimitate da poligoni vettoriali sopra il DEM ORIGINALE.  Viene trovato il punto più alto all'interno di ogni area.&#xa;&#xa;IMPORTANTE: deve esserci un campo di identificazione di ogni area con nome &quot;ID_PIFF&quot;.  Questo campo è obbligatorio per le successive elaborazioni altrimenti gli algoritmi futuri si bloccano." name="poly" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="OBSERVED points with aggregated data from SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP" name="qgis:executesql_8:OBSERVED_check" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="PROCESSED points with aggregated data from SUSCEPTIBILITY MAP" name="qgis:executesql_9:PROCESSED_check" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="There are three choices: &#xa;- ALL (analyzed all 7 rasters)&#xa;- ONLY ONE (analyzed only one raster model selected in WHICH RASTER)&#xa;- EXCLUDE ONLY ONE (analyzed all raster models except the one selected in WHICH RASTER)" name="select_raster_for_calculation" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the SLOPE of the area (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre)&#xa;" name="slope_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="A raster layer with the SOIL MOISTURE of the area. ATTENTION: the raster must have the same projection as the other raster files. It's optional. This file enhances the Topographic Wetness Index (TWI) layer produced by DTM of the area. This file is OPTIONAL." name="soil_moisture_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Soil Thickness Map - doubling, tripling or more the number of classes set by the programme" name="soil_thickness_map__more_categories_x2_x3_" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the SOIL THICKNESS MAP - STM - with values in meters (a Raster file you already have, or it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre)" name="soil_thickness_map_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The polygons of the SOURCES AREAS in which the highest elevation is to be found.&#xa;WARNING ---> &quot;ID_LIP&quot; is the mandatory name of the field for the identification of each area. ID_LIP is a Identification number of the area and must be an Integer field." name="sources_areas_vector" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Terrain Ruggedness Index - doubling, tripling or more the number of classes set by the programme" name="terrain_ruggedness_index__more_categories_x2_x3_" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="The raster file of THICKNESS MAP with the best risolution" name="thickness_map_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Topographic Wetness Index - doubling, tripling or more the number of classes set by the programme" name="topographic_wetness_index__more_categories_x2_x3_" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the TERRAIN RUGGEDNESS INDEX - TRI - of the area (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre)" name="tri_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="a raster file of the TOPOGRAPHIC WETNESS INDEX - TWI - of the area (it's created from the previous model ShaLIA_pre);" name="twi_raster" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="If the DTM grid is much larger than the landslide areas within the grid, it must be selected. For example, if the DTM has a resolution of 100x100 meters (area of 10,000 m²) and the landslide areas are much smaller, e.g., 100 or 200 m², the flag must be selected for a more accurate result. If, on the other hand, the DTM has a much lower resolution, e.g., 10x10 meters (area of 100 m²), the flag should not be selected. Choose based on the area data." name="very_large_raster_grid" type="QString"/>
    <Option value="Select the only raster model to be calculated or to be excluded. This is useless if “ALL” is selected in “SELECT RASTER FOR CALCULATION”" name="which_raster" type="QString"/>
  </Option>
